### SmartSurvey REST API walkthrough
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, Visual Studio and JetBrains HTTP clients.
# Start the app (dotnet run --project src/SmartSurvey.Web), then run the requests top to bottom.
# The JSON bodies live next to this file: survey-definition.json, submit-response.json, report-definition.json.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5057
@adminEmail = admin@smartsurvey.local
@adminPassword = Admin123!
@superAdminEmail = superadmin@smartsurvey.local
@superAdminPassword = SuperAdmin123!
# The seeded admin belongs to the workspace "Default workspace" (slug "default"); everything in steps 1–15
# happens inside that workspace. Steps 16+ show the super admin (System) and workspace endpoints.

### 1. Log in as the workspace administrator (bearer token)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Create a survey (always saved as a draft)
# @name createSurvey
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/surveys
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

< ./survey-definition.json

###
@surveyId = {{createSurvey.response.body.id}}
@slug = {{createSurvey.response.body.slug}}

### 3. Publish it
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/surveys/{{surveyId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Published" }

### 4. Respondent view: the workspace's public surveys (anonymous)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/surveys?workspace=default

### 5. Start the survey (definition + eligibility; a signed-in user also gets their draft)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/surveys/{{slug}}

### 6. Submit a response (anonymous allowed by this survey; validated with the conditional logic)
# Anonymous submissions must include the solved bot-protection challenge from step 5 ("challenge": salt, challenge,
# signature and the number n with sha256(salt + n) == challenge) — see DOCUMENTATION.md § Bot and spam protection.
# Signed-in callers (bearer token) are not challenged.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/surveys/{{surveyId}}/responses
Content-Type: application/json

< ./submit-response.json

### 7. Responses of the survey (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/surveys/{{surveyId}}/responses?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Raw export (csv | xlsx | json)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/surveys/{{surveyId}}/responses/export?format=csv
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Generate and save the automatic overview report
# @name defaultReport
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/default/{{surveyId}}?save=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@reportId = {{defaultReport.response.body.id}}

### 10. Run the report (tables, chart data, statistics as JSON)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/{{reportId}}/run
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Export the report (pdf | csv | txt | xlsx | json)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/{{reportId}}/export?format=pdf
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Build a custom report: preview first (nothing is saved) ...
# Replace "surveyId" in report-definition.json with the id from step 2 first.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

< ./report-definition.json

### 13. ... then save it
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

< ./report-definition.json

### 14. Dashboard KPIs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Audit log for the survey
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit?entityType=Survey&entityId={{surveyId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Log in as the super admin (runs the system; belongs to no workspace)
# @name superLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{superAdminEmail}}", "password": "{{superAdminPassword}}" }

###
@superToken = {{superLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 17. Branding: read (public) and change (super admins only — it is system-wide)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/branding

###
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/branding
Authorization: Bearer {{superToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productName": "Pulse Check", "tagline": "Listen better", "iconName": "bi-heart-pulse" }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/branding/reset
Authorization: Bearer {{superToken}}

### 18. Workspace settings of the signed-in admin's workspace (members may read, admins change)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspace
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspace
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Default workspace", "description": "Our surveys", "contactEmail": "team@example.com", "allowSelfRegistration": true, "showPublicSurveyList": true }

### 19. System overview and workspaces (super admin: figures only, never survey content)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/system/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{superToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/system/workspaces?search=&status=Active&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{superToken}}

### 20. Create a workspace with its first admin
# @name newWorkspace
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/system/workspaces
Authorization: Bearer {{superToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Field Research", "slug": "field-research", "adminEmail": "lead@field.example.com", "adminDisplayName": "Lead", "adminPassword": "Field123!" }

###
@workspaceId = {{newWorkspace.response.body.id}}

### 21. Disable it (members are signed out, survey links stop working, data is kept) — and enable it again
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/system/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{superToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Paused for the summer" }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/system/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{superToken}}

### 22. Accounts of every workspace, system settings and the system audit log
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/system/accounts?workspaceId={{workspaceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{superToken}}

###
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/system/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{superToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "allowWorkspaceSignup": true, "requireWorkspaceApproval": false, "supportEmail": "support@example.com" }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/system/audit?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{superToken}}

### 23. Self-service: anyone creates a workspace (and becomes its admin) or joins one with its link
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/settings

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/workspaces
Content-Type: application/json

{ "workspaceName": "Book Club", "displayName": "Robin", "email": "robin@example.com", "password": "BookClub123!" }

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/workspaces/book-club

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/workspaces/book-club/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "displayName": "Sam", "email": "sam@example.com", "password": "BookClub123!" }
